menu "Watering Can Pot Module Configuration"

    config WC_POT_MOISTURE_ADC_GPIO
        int "Soil moisture sensor ADC GPIO"
        range 0 54
        default 19
        help
            GPIO wired to the capacitive soil moisture sensor's analog
            output, via the Hat2-Bus header. Must be an ADC-capable pin --
            on esp32p4, that's GPIO 16-23 (ADC1) or 49-54 (ADC2). GPIO19 on
            the Hat2-Bus header is now confirmed correct on real hardware
            (a first wiring attempt landed on GND/3.3V instead -- misread
            silkscreen -- and was caught by a pegged, out-of-range reading;
            after fixing the wiring, readings correctly track wet vs. dry).
            Other Hat2-Bus pins earmarked for future sensors are still
            unconfirmed -- verify with a multimeter/continuity test before
            trusting the silkscreen for those.

    config WC_POT_MOISTURE_RAW_DRY
        int "ADC raw reading calibrated as 0% (driest)"
        range 0 4095
        default 2800
        help
            Raw ADC counts measured with the sensor in open air -- the
            driest calibration point. Measured on hardware: ~2780-2834
            across several seconds of readings. Air (rather than bone-dry
            soil) is the standard "dry" calibration point for capacitive
            moisture sensors -- the sensor can't distinguish "no medium"
            from "bone-dry medium" since both have near-identical
            dielectric properties. If a real dry-soil reading ever falls
            outside the dry/wet range here, re-measure and adjust.

    config WC_POT_MOISTURE_RAW_WET
        int "ADC raw reading calibrated as 100% (wettest)"
        range 0 4095
        default 1478
        help
            Raw ADC counts measured with the sensor fully submerged in
            water -- the wettest calibration point. Measured on hardware:
            ~1461-1495 across several seconds of readings. For reference,
            moist (but not submerged) potting soil measured ~2000-2024 on
            this same sensor, landing comfortably between the two bounds
            here.

endmenu
